Scope of this licence

The MIT licence above covers this project's own code and documents. It does not replace the licences of the
third-party software the experimental Windows VR runtime builds on and adapts:

- The Steam client code under `visionos-windows-vr/Sources/Steam` and `third-party/steam-native` is adapted from
  Madeira (copyright Jfishin and 125hz) and stays under GPL-3.0-or-later with the Madeira Converter Exception;
  the full text is in `third-party/steam-native/COPYING` and `LICENSE-EXCEPTION.md`.
- Madeira, Wine, FEX-Emu, DXMT, OpenComposite, OpenVR, OpenXR-SDK, the ALVR visionOS client, StikDebug/StikJIT,
  idevice, LLVM and llvm-mingw, and the libraries Madeira links, keep their own licences and copyright notices.
  Their authors are credited, with licences and how each is used, in THIRD-PARTY.md.
- The patches in `windows-vr-openxr/patches/` and `windows-runtime-plugin/patches/` modify those projects and are
  provided under the licence of the project each one patches.

Anyone who distributes a built Windows VR app must also meet those licences, including providing complete
corresponding source for the GPL and LGPL parts. No game content, Valve client binary or Apple proprietary
library is part of this repository.
